\section{Simulation Execution \& Orchestration Pipeline}

\subsection{Master Execution Cycle}

The simulation runner coordinates the multi-scale PDE substrate, immune CTSHA engine, and Hamiltonian stability controller. Let $t$ denote the global simulation clock and $\Delta t$ the discrete timestep satisfying all CFL bounds.

\begin{enumerate}
    \item \textbf{Initialization:} Load virtual patient profile, GI geometry, mucosal receptor density $\rho_{\mathrm{muc}}(x)$, and physiological field $P_H(x,0)$.
    \item \textbf{Distributed Allocation:} Initialize MPI domains, assign PDE partitions, and allocate GPU buffers for surrogate neural modules.
    \item \textbf{Main Simulation Loop:}
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item Solve GI fluid dynamics and peristaltic velocity field $v(x,t)$.
        \item Update pH gradients and enzymatic kinetics $\mu(x,t)$.
        \item Integrate pill dissolution PDE for $C_p(x,t)$.
        \item Integrate antigen transport PDE for $C_a(x,t)$.
        \item Evaluate immune CTSHA transition equation
        \[
        \frac{d\mathbf{P}}{dt} = \mathbf{Q}(\mathbf{X}(t))\,\mathbf{P}(t).
        \]
        \item Evaluate Lyapunov stability condition
        \[
        \frac{d}{dt} V_{\mathrm{Lyap}} \le -\gamma \|\delta\mathbf{q}\|^2.
        \]
    \end{enumerate}
    \item \textbf{Stability Branch:}
    \begin{itemize}
        \item If unstable: apply damping correction to $\dot{\mathbf{q}}$ and $\dot{\mathbf{p}}$.
        \item If stable: stream telemetry to visualization HUD.
    \end{itemize}
    \item \textbf{Clock Advancement:} Update $t \leftarrow t + \Delta t$.
\end{enumerate}

