\section{Real-Time Telemetry \& Validation Metrics}

\subsection{Mass Balance Verification}

At each timestep $t$, the total mass is validated:

\[
M_{\mathrm{total}}(t)
=
\int_0^L C_p(x,t)\,dx
+
\int_0^L C_a(x,t)\,dx
+
M_{\mathrm{absorbed}}(t),
\]

with numerical leakage constrained by

\[
\left| M_{\mathrm{total}}(t+\Delta t) - M_{\mathrm{total}}(t) \right|
< 10^{-6}.
\]

\subsection{Compute Pipeline Performance}

The PDE solver (C++ core) and surrogate neural network (LibTorch) exchange data via asynchronous buffers. Real-time constraints require:

\[
\mathrm{FPS} \ge 60,
\qquad
\mathrm{Load}_{\mathrm{GPU}} + \mathrm{Load}_{\mathrm{CPU}} \le \mathrm{Budget}_{\mathrm{RT}}.
\]

Telemetry includes:
\begin{itemize}
    \item PDE convergence residuals,
    \item CTSHA transition entropy,
    \item Hamiltonian drift $\Delta\mathcal{H}$,
    \item CFL compliance indicators.
\end{itemize}